title: vmul.f32: a product just below 2^-126 is flushed (sign kept); a NaN lane gives the default NaN
ref: A8.8 VMUL (floating-point) T1 (Advanced SIMD); A2.7 FPMul() with StandardFPSCRValue() (DN, FZ, round to nearest); FPRound(): FZ = 1 and exponent < -126 (decided on the exact value) gives FPZero(sign); FPProcessNaN() with DN = 1 gives 0x7FC00000

[code]
42ff110d    vmul.f32 d16, d2, d1
7047        bx lr

[in]
s2 = 0x00800000     # 2^-126
s3 = f32:2.0
s4 = 0xBF7FFFFF     # -(1 - 2^-24): the product is -(2^-126 - 2^-150), which would round to -2^-126
s5 = 0x7F800001     # a signalling NaN

[out]
d16 = 0x7FC0000080000000
